  "id": "Compound::DB00763 - Gene::1571",
  "verbalization": "Methimazole exhibits a strong binding interaction with Cyp2a6 and Cyp2d6, which are both involved in the metabolism of arachidonic acid. This binding leads to the participation of these enzymes in the epoxygenation of arachidonic acid, a process that ultimately results in the activation of Cyp2e1. The evidence suggests that Methimazole indirectly influences Cyp2e1 through its effects on Cyp2a6 and Cyp2d6, which are part of the same metabolic pathway. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a robust, mechanistically supported relationship, with Methimazole acting as a modulator of Cyp2e1 via the arachidonic acid metabolism pathway. The presence of multiple pathways converging on Cyp2e1 underscores the importance of this enzyme in the metabolic response to Methimazole, and the integrated evidence supports a role for Methimazole in modulating Cyp2e1 through the epoxygenation of arachidonic acid.",
